# Paths from CLAUDE.md "Nicht ohne Rückfrage ändern", plus what guards them.
# GitHub requests a review from the owner on every PR that touches them. With a single maintainer the ruleset on main
# does not require code owner approval (GitHub does not let authors approve their own PR); this file documents
# ownership and becomes binding as soon as a second reviewer exists.

# Generated migrations and snapshots: only via the db-change skill.
/drizzle/                  @benschuetze

# Expected values and their templates: set by rule, never by a model.
/evals/belege.json         @benschuetze
/evals/generate.ts         @benschuetze

# Accounts and tax keys need a fachliche review.
/app/lib/skr03.ts          @benschuetze

# CI, workflows, this file: actions pinned to SHA, minimal permissions.
/.github/                  @benschuetze

# The guardrails and the reviewers' rules.
/.claude/settings.json     @benschuetze
/.claude/hooks/            @benschuetze
/.claude/agents/           @benschuetze
/CLAUDE.md                 @benschuetze
